  to make a Roman temple with it I'm just  gonna look at the pieces and see if they  can fit into my plan and then if they do  you can find some like interesting way  to fit them into that plan I think it's  just a nice way to get more  out-of-the-box thinking going to try  with different themes of the with the  pieces in the game and just overall get  more unique and creative things out of  it it's a lot more fun for me personally  as well because don't you so rigidly  have to follow where the game gives you  it's more about breaking what the game  has and seeing what you can actually do  with the game though I wouldn't  especially recommend trying to make  roofs out of doors it's the idea that  counts there are many different uses for  many different  in the game and will never ever find all  of the uses for all the objects but it's  a lot of fun to just find new little  tricks and ways to use objects in ways  that they're not really meant to and  just keep building on that I think  that's a good way to improve your  building as well if you compare my  current building to what I was making in  grizzly Valley episode 1 like regardless  of whether you think what I build is  good I think you can already see that in  others huge leaps forward in using  certain pieces and it all just kind of  sticks together because in the end and  this is something that I cannot you know  ignore and something that I do have to  say as much of cliche as it is  experience and practice are a lot and I  didn't talk about them in this video  because well they seem kind of  self-explanatory but they are really a  lot and it's it's through this that you  just kind of get better at the game and  I think just personally a good way to  get this to actually let the experience  help you out and get better over time is  to look at the game exactly the way that  I do though I'm obviously always open  for other feedback on this or other  people's comments or how other people  look at the game and play the game and  enjoy the game so I'm definitely up for  some discussion in the comment section  as well but these are just my thoughts  and it's so yeah go get that experience  because experience always counts no  matter how shitty whatever it is that  you're making you at least made  something and it will make everything  that you make from that point onward at  least a little bit better even if you  remove whatever you were working on it's  always progress and it's never a waste  of time and also mention just to bring  out my favorite quote of all time time  you enjoy wasting isn't waste of time  and neither is any kind of time that  you're just doing whatever in a game  like this waste of time because whatever  you're doing you always get better and  the things you'll do in the future just  because it'll build on it anyway this  was my little solo podcast of looking  too deep into games with silver ATS  thank you for listening and if you want  to have more stupidly deep  readings into video games with silver  ads make sure to leave the comments and  in all seriousness though I'm not really  sure if I'm gonna do this much more  often in the future but if you do  appreciate it some feedback would be  awesome Don the other hand if you think  this is totally stupid that's cool too  and you can always leave a comment about  what you kind of do want my videos to  look like but yeah thanks for watching  in any case whether you hate or love  this video and I hope to see you guys in  the next video whatever it'll be
 

